      "writtenOn": "2026-06-15T16:35:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we push this down to `SkPDFGradientShader::Make`?  I think it could return an invalid indirect reference for non-opaque stops, and then we fall back here.  That would also provide a general fallback mechanism if gradient conversion fails for whatever other reason (prolly not possible atm).\n\nThen `has_alpha` can be a local static, and we can also be more aggressive with some of the checks (e.g. assert non-null gradient, assert !\u003d kNone gradient type, assert stop count \u003e 0 etc).\n\n```\n    if (SkPDFIndirectReference gradientShader \u003d\n            SkPDFGradientShader::Make(doc, shader, canvasTransform, surfaceBBox)) {\n        return gradientShader;\n    }\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 346,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 349,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "aa160a8cbe2c18cfe53b2b98b7ff5e0c3e4d9f72",
